# Day 38 secrets audit — neither of these was ever actually excluded.
# uploads/ holds real user-submitted documents (app/core/storage.py's
# UPLOAD_DIR) — not secrets exactly, but user content that has no
# business in git history. secrets/ is where the README has always
# told people to put the Google service-account JSON key (see the
# Day-23-era setup docs) — without this entry, anyone who followed
# that instruction literally and then ran a bare `git add .` would
# commit a real credential.
uploads/
secrets/